    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-problem-1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "By turning the $x$ at the front into $(x+1-1)$, or otherwise, show that\n\n$$f(x)=(x+1)^6-(x+1)^5.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x(x+1)^5=(x+1)^6-(x+1)^5$ by writing $x=(x+1)-1$ and distributing.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=\\bigl((x+1)-1\\bigr)(x+1)^5\\\\f(x)&=(x+1)^6-(x+1)^5.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-problem-1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, differentiate $f(x)=x(x+1)^5$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)=(6x+1)(x+1)^4$",
          "worked": "Differentiate the two powers from part (a). The inner derivative of $x+1$ is $1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=6(x+1)^5-5(x+1)^4\\\\f'(x)&=(x+1)^4\\bigl(6(x+1)-5\\bigr)\\\\f'(x)&=(6x+1)(x+1)^4.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      }
    ]
